{"complete":true,"school_name":"Pennsylvania State University-Main Campus","town_name":"University Park","boards":[{"complete":true,"school_name":"Pennsylvania State University-Main Campus","town_name":"University Park","template_id":"college-first-weekend","title":"Your First Weekend at Pennsylvania State University, Shared as Cards","description":"A low-pressure, under-21-safe first-weekend sequence through University Park landmarks, arts, campus resources, and a Friday-night treat.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"subject_id":"psu-old-main-frescoes","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Old Main Land-Grant Frescoes","title":"Friday afternoon — Start at Old Main","subtitle":"Old Main lobby, University Park","notes":"Step inside during weekday visitor hours to view the land-grant frescoes, then use the lobby as a visual anchor before continuing across campus.","short_summary":"A historic first stop centered on the murals inside Penn State’s landmark administration building.","evidence_claim":"Penn State says visitors can view Old Main’s land-grant frescoes weekdays from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.; the mural installation covers more than 1,300 square feet.","source_url":"https://www.psu.edu/news/campus-life/story/hidden-gems-land-grant-frescoes-old-main","source_title":"Hidden Gems: The land-grant frescoes at Old Main","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2024-09-18","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Penn State states that visitors can stop in weekdays, 8 a.m.–5 p.m., to view the frescoes.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"psu-nittany-lion-shrine","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Nittany Lion Shrine","title":"Friday afternoon — Find the Nittany Lion Shrine","subtitle":"University Park campus landmark","notes":"Walk over for an exterior photo and take a moment to orient yourself; keep this stop simple and avoid climbing on the sculpture or surrounding rocks.","short_summary":"A named campus sculpture and recognizable outdoor meeting point.","evidence_claim":"Penn State identifies the Nittany Lion Shrine at University Park as a landmark that draws visitors and is recognized as one of Pennsylvania’s most photographed landmarks.","source_url":"https://www.psu.edu/about/nittany-lion-shrine","source_title":"Nittany Lion Shrine | History","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor landmark; follow posted campus rules and respect the sculpture.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"psu-hub-engagement-space","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Student Engagement Network Engagement Space","title":"Friday late afternoon — Browse opportunities at the HUB","subtitle":"HUB-Robeson Center, University Park","notes":"Stop by the Engagement Space to identify one organization, project, or opportunity worth following up on after your first weekend.","short_summary":"A campus-based place to turn early curiosity into a concrete next step.","evidence_claim":"The Student Engagement Network says its Engagement Space is in the HUB-Robeson Center and is equipped with tools and staff to help students identify goals and available opportunities.","source_url":"https://sen.psu.edu/engagement-space/","source_title":"Engagement Space at University Park","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The space is in the HUB-Robeson Center; ask staff about current availability and programs.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"psu-hub-galleries","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"HUB-Robeson Galleries","title":"Friday early evening — See the HUB galleries","subtitle":"First floor of the HUB-Robeson Center","notes":"Take